1: # Brief assembler (super-code)
2: 
3: super-code's coordinator dispatches the assembler with this file's absolute path and the values of
4: the bracketed parameters (the `assemblePrompt` builder in coordinator.js). Model tier: `mechanical`.
5: Everything below the line is addressed to the dispatched agent.
6: 
7: ---
8: 
9: The assembler gathers inputs into one directory with tool calls and judges nothing: no verdicts, no
10: severity, no summaries beyond the extraction each section defines. Write only inside [OUT_DIR];
11: never edit another file, never commit, and don't spawn subagents.
12: 
13: Parameters: [CONSUMER], [INSTANCE], [OUT_DIR], [WORKTREE], [BASE], [HEAD], [SECTIONS] (one
14: `name: definition` line per digest section), [CLUSTERS] (yes or no), [THRESHOLD] (tokens),
15: [ASSEMBLED_SIZE] (the size script's command), [LEDGER], [WORKSPACE], [SPEC_PATHS].
16: 
17: 1. `cd [WORKTREE]`. Review consumers (`final-review`, `roast-code`) receive captured commit
18:    identities as [BASE] and [HEAD]; verify both with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`.
19:    Other consumers resolve command-valued inputs once before collecting their data.
20:    Empty the instance directory first:
21:    `rm -rf [OUT_DIR] && mkdir -p [OUT_DIR]/slices`.
22: 2. `git diff --stat [BASE]..[HEAD] > [OUT_DIR]/diffstat.txt`.
23: 3. Write `[OUT_DIR]/digest.md` with one `## <name>` heading per [SECTIONS] line, in that order, each
24:    built only from the source its definition names. Copy; don't paraphrase or rank. A source that has
25:    nothing gets the line `none`.
26: 4. Slices: one file per changed source file, `git diff [BASE]..[HEAD] -- <file>` written to
27:    `[OUT_DIR]/slices/<path with each / replaced by __>.diff`.
28:    Open source with `git show [HEAD]:<path>` so a concurrent caller advance cannot change it.
29: 5. When [CLUSTERS] is yes, group the changed files by import and call edges between them (an edge
30:    when one changed file imports or calls a symbol another defines), else by top-level directory,
31:    never by a count of files. Write `[OUT_DIR]/clusters.json`:
32:    `{"changed": ["<repo path>", …], "clusters": [{"name": "<name>", "files": ["<repo path>", …], "slices": ["slices/<file>", …]}]}`
33:    with every changed file in exactly one cluster and each cluster's slices the ones for its files.
34:    Each `name` is a slug: lowercase letters, digits and `-` only (e.g. `run-marker`, `hooks`), unique in the file.
35: 6. Run `[ASSEMBLED_SIZE] [OUT_DIR] --threshold [THRESHOLD]`. When [CLUSTERS] is yes and it prints
36:    `fits: no`, re-cluster once by subdirectory each cluster printed as `cluster-fits: <name> no`
37:    (update `clusters.json`), then run
38:    `[ASSEMBLED_SIZE] [OUT_DIR] --threshold [THRESHOLD] --clusters-required`.
39: 7. Relay the LAST run of the size script unchanged: `exit` is its exit code (any exit code, including
40:    3 and 4, is relayed, not fixed), `fits` its `fits:` line verbatim, `clusterFits` its
41:    `cluster-fits:` lines verbatim (an empty list when it printed none), `clusters` the number of
42:    clusters in `clusters.json` (0 when none), `dir` is [OUT_DIR]. Set `cause` only when you could not
43:    finish a step, naming it.

